<title>UK: Cera Bank sets 2.0 bln Lfr structured 7-year bond.</title>
<headline>Cera Bank sets 2.0 bln Lfr structured 7-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Cera Bank Luxembourg, Banque et Caisse d'Epargne de l&quot;Etat.</p>
<p> BORROWER   CERA BANK</p>
<p> AMT    2.0 BLN LUF   COUPON     *4.50     MATURITY  **31.DEC.03</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.45    PAY DATE 30/31.DEC.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K)  50-250</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    LUX	 TAX PROVS   STANDARD PRAECIPUUM  0.25</p>
<p> NOTES	*TO 31.DEC.00, THEN PAYS YIELD OF THE THREE-YEAR OLO</p>
<p>		 LESS 0.375 PCT WITH A MINIMUM OF 6.50 PCT</p>
<p>	     **PUTTABLE ON 31.DEC.00 AT PAR WITH A YIELD TO PUT OF</p>
<p>		 4.10 PCT OR A MINIMUM YIELD OF 5.02 PCT TO MATURITY</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
